      "rev_n_3_631856_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_631856_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_631856",
        "thought_text": "The `is_transposition` function incorrectly returns `True` immediately if the first notes of both melodies match, bypassing the necessary check that the interval between consecutive notes remains constant throughout the entire sequence. This logic must be fixed to verify that the shift amount is consistent for all notes, not just the first one, before confirming a transposition.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_631856_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_5800079025",
        "created_at": 1794508138.3733807
      },
      "rev_n_1_561c43_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_561c43_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_561c43",
        "thought_text": "The inversion logic incorrectly calculates the expected note by subtracting the interval from the first note without accounting for the 12-tone wrap-around (modulo 12), causing valid inverted notes to fail the comparison. The reasoning must be updated to apply modulo 12 arithmetic when calculating the inverted note's integer value to ensure it wraps correctly within the 0-11 range.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_561c43_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_341ed69322",
        "created_at": 1794508164.2430305
      },
      "rev_n_4_2e6ff0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_2e6ff0_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_2e6ff0",
        "thought_text": "Implement a mapping from note names to integers 0-11, then verify Transposition by checking if the difference between corresponding notes is constant modulo 12.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-5859753152638814737",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794508195.9863014
